Files: src/lora/*
       include/phy/lora/*
       tests/lora_offline_test.cpp
Copyright: 2026 Roy C. Gross
           Joachim Tapparel, EPFL Telecommunication Circuits Laboratory, and gr-lora_sdr contributors
           Pieter Robyns, Peter Quax, Wim Lamotte, William Thenaers, and gr-lora contributors
License: GPL-3.0-only
Comment: Portions of the bit-level LoRa coding chain (whitening sequence,
 explicit header checksum, Hamming FEC, diagonal interleaver) and analytic
 chirp modulation adapt conventions and tables from gr-lora_sdr
 (https://github.com/tapparelj/gr-lora_sdr), which was inspired by gr-lora
 (https://github.com/rpp0/gr-lora). Chirp-spread-spectrum demodulation
 concepts (oversampled dechirp spectrum folding, argmax peak tracking)
 build on published LoRa SDR physical layer implementations from EPFL
 (Tapparel et al., 2020, 2024) and Hasselt University (Robyns et al., 2017).
 Upstream repositories are distributed under GPL-3.0.

